", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Georgia remains one of the closest states on the presidential map. The state's partisan lean favors Republicans by about a point, and with the incumbent president term-limited, neither party starts with an incumbency advantage. No statewide polls of the race have been published, and no expert ratings are available yet, so fundamentals are doing the work.\n\nThe result is a genuine tossup, with Republicans holding a very slight edge on paper. Recent headlines have focused on Democratic speculation about Jon Ossoff's future rather than the presidential contest itself, and Georgia's pending search for a new voting system for 2028 adds procedural uncertainty. Until credible polling or ratings arrive, the race should be treated as effectively even, with wide uncertainty about where the national environment will land.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4567, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4683, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.467, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4627, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4625, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4629, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4605, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4643, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.455, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4633, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4576, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4404, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p